{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azure-cognitive-services/vision/read","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:03.034Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azure-cognitive-services/vision/read/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azure-cognitive-services/vision/read/about"},"readme":"## About\n\n[Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services) is a set of APIs, SDKs and container images that enables developers to integrate ready-made AI directly into their applications. Azure AI services contains a broad set of capabilities including text analytics; facial detection, speech and vision recognition; natural language understanding, and more.\n\nContainer support in Azure AI services allow developers to use the same rich APIs that are available in Azure but with the flexibility that comes with containers. See [Container support in Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services-containers) for details.\n\nRead is part of [Azure AI Vision](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/services/cognitive-services/computer-vision/). The Read OCR container allows you to extract printed and handwritten text from images and documents with support for JPEG, PNG, BMP, PDF, and TIFF file formats. For more information, see the [Read API documentation](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cognitive-services/computer-vision/concept-recognizing-text##read-api).\n\n> Note: The Latest tag points to 3.2\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `latest`\ndocker pull mcr.microsoft.com/azure-cognitive-services/vision/read\n\n## Related repositories\n\n+ [Azure AI services Images](https://hub.docker.com/_/microsoft-azure-cognitive-services): Azure AI services is a set of APIs, SDKs and container images that enables developers to integrate ready-made AI directly into their applications.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSee the [configuration documentation](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cognitive-services/computer-vision/computer-vision-resource-container-config) for how to configure this image.\n\n## Usage\n\nSee the [How-to](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cognitive-services/computer-vision/computer-vision-how-to-install-containers) for how to use this image.\n\nAlso see the [set of samples](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2043312&clcid=0x409) to help getting started with Azure AI services.\n\n## Related Information\n\n+ [Optical Character Recognition (OCR)](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cognitive-services/computer-vision/concept-recognizing-text)\n+ [Azure AI Vision Azure Cognitive Service](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/services/cognitive-services/computer-vision)\n+ [Container Support in Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services-containers)\n+ [Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services)\n+ [Azure Portal](http://portal.azure.com)\n\n## Support\n\nReport feedback or issues on [Stack Overflow](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2056278) using tag azure-cognitive-services.\n\n## License\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)\n\n\nNotice: Copyright © Microsoft Corporation 2020. This Azure AI services Container image is made available to you under the [terms governing your subscription to Microsoft Azure Services](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2018657) (including the [Online Services Terms](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2018760)). If you do not have a valid Azure subscription, then you may not use this container.","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-11T08:55:33.80412+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"Other","links":[{"name":"licence","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/licensing/terms/product/ForOnlineServices/EAEAS"}],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"639K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes"